      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three low-pressure ways to start shifting your evenings: 1. **Establish a regular \"third place\":** Pick a local coffee shop, library branch, or neighborhood spot and visit at roughly the same time once or twice a week. Becoming a familiar regular helps you feel connected to the area without the pressure of forced socializing.\n2. **Find an activity-based group:** Look up a casual run or walk club, a board game night, an adult rec league, or a volunteer shift. Having an activity at the center makes talking to new people much more natural.\n3. **Turn one night into an exploration walk:** Pick a nearby street, market, or park you haven’t checked out yet and explore it on foot. It gives the evening a clear purpose and helps you get your bearings in the new city. Pick whichever one feels easiest to try first.",
